---
const rows: [string, string, string, string, string][] = [
  ["How sound is made", "A generative model renders audio from a text prompt", "Sliders and randomise buttons over one synth patch", "A human enters notes into pattern grids", "The agent writes a source file in a text notation that SEGAN compiles"],
  ["Sound is stored as", "MP3/WAV files", "Parameter sets, or exported WAVs", "Module files (.ftm, .fur, …) + exports", "Text in git: diffable, reviewable, editable by hand or by agent"],
  ["What it makes", "SFX, ambience, voice, full songs", "Short SFX", "Music (and SFX by hand)", "SFX, layered and phased; looping music with variants and stems"],
  ["Cost / access", "Credits or subscriptions, cloud, account", "Free, mostly in the browser", "Free (some open source)", "Free, MIT, offline"],
  ["Realism", "Best of the four: recorded-sounding audio and vocals", "Retro synth only", "Chip / synth (sample playback in some)", "Synth only: chiptune and 80s synth; no samples, no vocals"],
  ["Consistency across a game", "Per prompt", "Per sound", "Per module", "One shared kit palette, mix, room and loudness targets; change one setting, every asset re-renders"],
  ["Quality checks", "None", "None", "Your ears", "Lint the agent reads and fixes (lead-in silence, loop clicks, clipping, aliasing, clashes, loudness), and listen sheets it can look at"],
  ["Engine output", "Audio files", "WAV", "WAV / NSF / chip formats", "WAVs with smpl loop points, manifest.json for any engine, Godot .import loops, randomizers and synchronized stems"],
  ["Agent access", "APIs; ElevenLabs has an official MCP server", "ZzFX's sounds are short code arrays", "None", "Claude skill, MCP server (22 tools), --json CLI"],
  ["Deterministic", "No", "Yes", "Yes", "Yes: byte-identical builds"],
];
---

<section id="compare">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">How it compares</span>
    <h2>Four kinds of tool</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Facts as of October 2026, from each tool's own documentation. Pick what fits your game.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"></th>
            <th scope="col">AI audio generators<small>ElevenLabs Sound Effects, Stable Audio, Suno, Udio</small></th>
            <th scope="col">Procedural SFX tools<small>sfxr / jsfxr / bfxr, ChipTone, ZzFX</small></th>
            <th scope="col">Trackers<small>FamiTracker, Furnace</small></th>
            <th scope="col" class="us">SEGAN</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            rows.map(([k, a, b, c, d]) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{k}</th>
                <td>{a}</td>
                <td>{b}</td>
                <td>{c}</td>
                <td class="us">{d}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="where">
      <b>Where SEGAN loses:</b> it isn't a recording studio or a composer. For realistic foley, orchestral
      scores or vocals, a sample library or an audio generator is better, and SEGAN can't judge taste: a
      human has to listen. SEGAN wins on a whole game's worth of retro-synth sounds and loops that match,
      loop cleanly, and change together.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-top: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 920px;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  thead th {
    font: 0.85rem var(--font-pixel);
    background: var(--panel);
  }
  thead small {
    display: block;
    font: 0.75rem var(--font-body);
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  tbody th {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
    width: 13%;
  }
  td {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .us {
    color: var(--text);
    background: rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.09);
  }
  thead .us {
    color: var(--wave);
  }
  tbody tr:last-child > * {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .where {
    margin-top: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  .where b {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
